  "card": {
    "title": "PR search is flaky — race condition between input and API results (pasted PR numbers return wrong matches)",
    "type": "feature",
    "scope": "# Summary\n\nPR search is unreliable: pasting a PR number returns seemingly random results, and the correct results only appear after deleting a character and re-typing it. This points to a race condition where search responses arrive out of order relative to the current input and stale responses are not discarded.\n\n# Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Open PR search.\n2. Paste a PR number (e.g. `049`) into the search bar.\n\nExpected: Results contain PRs where `049` appears in the title or the PR number `049`.\nActual: Unrelated results are returned (e.g. PRs containing `050` and `031`); deleting a character and re-adding it is required to get the expected results. Search feels flaky in general.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Pasting a PR number returns only matching results (title or PR number) without needing to edit the input\n- [ ] Rapid typing or pasting never displays results from a stale/earlier query\n- [ ] Searching `049` returns PRs matching `049`, not `050`/`031`\n- [ ] Search input is debounced and out-of-order/stale responses are discarded (or in-flight requests aborted)\n\n# Dev Hints\n\n* Likely cause: in-flight requests aren't cancelled/ignored, so a later paste/keystroke's results get overwritten by an earlier request that resolves last.\n* Fixes to consider: tag each request with its query and ignore responses that don't match the current input; use `AbortController` to cancel superseded requests; add input debounce.",
